course: dictionary
lesson: 5698
title: Logic: clear, careful thinking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Logic is careful, clear thinking. Each step follows from the one before, so you reach a sensible answer. When you solve a puzzle, you use logic: you read the clues, test each one, and check that your answer fits them all.
explain: Logic can also mean the reason or sense behind something. «I don't see the logic of that plan» means the speaker cannot understand why anyone would make that plan. They are asking what the sense in it is.
explain: Logic also has special meanings in maths and computing. In maths it is the study of correct reasoning. In coding, words like «and», «or» and «not» are logic: a computer checks what is true or false, then picks its next step. Something «against all logic» is surprising or silly.
fact: Logic means careful, clear thinking where each step follows from the one before.
fact: A «logic puzzle» gives you clues, and you use them to work out who has which pet or which number is hidden.
fact: Logic is also the study of correct reasoning, a part of maths and philosophy.
fact: «There's no logic in it» means the idea does not make sense.
fact: A computer follows logic: it checks true or false steps, such as «if … then … else».
exercise: «I don't see the logic of that plan.» What does logic mean here? | *The reason or sense behind the plan | A kind of food | The name of the person who made it | The price of the plan
exercise: Which phrase means something is surprising or silly? | logic puzzle | the logic behind it | *against all logic | use your logic
exercise: Mia says logic is only for maths. What is the best answer? | Yes, logic means being very loud | Yes, logic is only a maths word | No, logic is a type of weather | *No, logic is also clear thinking in stories, puzzles and computers
test: Why can't someone who always tells the truth say «I am a liar»? | Because they are too shy to say it | Because the sentence is too long | Because liars cannot speak at all | *Because saying it would be false, which breaks their own rule
test: «Aristotle studied everything from animals to poetry and logic.» Which of these did Aristotle study? | Only cooking | *Logic | Only the stars | Only music
exam: Which of these is true about logic? | *It is careful, clear thinking where each step follows the one before | It means being very loud | It is only a word for feelings | It is a type of cake
